speaker: Emily Spahn
---
bio:

Emily Spahn (she/her) is a coder and data scientist based out of Seattle. She is a licensed civil engineer and has interests in machine learning, public data, dogs, and using technology for the greater good. She currently works at DroneSeed on software to make reforestation scalable.
---
title: The Ethics of Aesthetics: Classifying Personal Care Products on Saftey and Substance
---
abstract:
Modern skin care products often contain many ingredients with complex names. Let’s develop a system to parse an ingredient label and provide both a breakdown of the ingredient sources and the overall safety of the product given its ingredients, so we can become more informed consumers.
